World War II had ended only three months prior. It wouldn't be long before the Sodder's second oldest son, Joseph, who had been serving in the US Army, returned home to Fayetteville, West Virginia. As the night wore on, two of the older Sodder sons, John and George Jr, retired to bed. They had spent the day helping their father with work and were tired. The pair headed up into the attic, which was used as a space for the many Sodder children to sleep. The attic was divided into two rooms and accessible via a set of stairs. George Sr. also went to bed at this time, in the master bedroom on the main floor.
第二次世界大战在仅仅三个月前刚刚结束。要不了多久，索德家的二儿子约瑟夫就会从美国陆军退伍，回到西弗吉尼亚州费耶特维尔的家中。夜深了，索德家的两个大儿子约翰和小乔治上床睡觉了。他们花了一整天时间帮父亲干活，已经累了。两人上到了阁楼，那里是索德家众多孩子睡觉的地方。阁楼被隔成两个房间，可以通过一组楼梯上去。老乔治此时也上床睡觉了，睡在主楼层的主卧室里。

4
00:02:28.000 --> 00:03:29.000
His wife followed shortly thereafter at around 10.30pm, taking their three-year-old daughter, Sylvia, with her. The other Sodder children, Morris, Martha, Lewis, Jenny and Betty, continued to play with their new toys. Marion lay on the couch, keeping an eye on the youngsters who ranged from 5 to 14 years old. At about 12.30am, Jenny woke to the sound of the telephone ringing in her husband's study next to the master bedroom. She got up to answer it and was met on the line by a woman whose voice she didn't recognise. In the background were the sounds of laughing and chatter and of glass clinking. The caller asked for someone who didn't reside at the Sodder residence. When Jenny told her she had the wrong number, the woman laughed strangely before hanging up.
他的妻子紧随其后，大约在晚上10点30分上楼，并带上了他们三岁的女儿西尔维娅。索德家的其他孩子莫里斯、玛莎、刘易斯、珍妮和贝蒂则继续玩着他们的新玩具。马里昂躺在沙发上，照看着年龄从5岁到14岁不等的小家伙们。大约凌晨12点30分，珍妮被主卧室隔壁她丈夫书房里的电话铃声吵醒。她起来接电话，电话那头是一个她听不出来的女人的声音。背景音里传来欢笑声、聊天声以及玻璃碰撞声。来电者询问了一个并不住在索德家的人。当珍妮告诉她打错电话时，那个女人发出奇怪的笑声，然后挂断了电话。

5
00:03:29.000 --> 00:04:53.000
As she left the study, Jenny realised the lights were still on in the family room where the children had been playing. The front door was also unlocked. Usually the job of the last family member to go to bed, Jenny walked past Marion who was sleeping on the sofa and locked the door and turned off the lights. Assuming all her other children were asleep in the attic, Jenny went back to bed. A light sleeper, Jenny was disrupted again 30 minutes later at around 1am on Christmas morning. What sounded like a hard rubber ball landed on the tar and wood roof of the family's cottage. It rolled down the roof. Then there was silence. Exhausted, Jenny ignored the noise, rolling over and going back to sleep.
当她离开书房时，珍妮发现孩子们刚才玩耍的家庭活动室里的灯还亮着。前门也没有锁。这通常是家里最后一个人睡觉时要做的事，珍妮走过睡在沙发上的马里昂，锁上了门，关掉了灯。珍妮以为其他孩子都在阁楼上睡着了，于是便回房睡觉了。作为一个觉浅的人，珍妮在30分钟后，也就是圣诞节早晨1点左右再次被惊醒。有什么听起来像硬橡胶球的东西落在了这家人小木屋的柏油木质屋顶上。它从屋顶滚了下来。接着是一片寂静。筋疲力尽的珍妮没有理会这个声音，翻个身又睡着了。

6
00:04:53.000 --> 00:05:54.000
30 minutes later at 1.30am, Jenny woke to the smell of smoke. She followed the trail and found it was coming from George's study which was on fire. She raced back to her room and roused George. He in turn woke Marion who was still sleeping on the sofa. She took three-year-old Sylvia outside to safety. Jenny yelled frantically at the bottom of the attic stairs for the seven children above to come down. The fire was moving quickly and was already starting to take hold of the stairs. After what seemed an eternity, John and George Jr. made their way down. Their hair was singed from the flames. Meanwhile, George Sr. attempted to call the local fire department only to find the phone line to the Sotter House was dead.
30分钟后，即凌晨1点30分，珍妮闻到了一股烟味。她顺着气味找去，发现气味来自正在着火的乔治的书房。她跑回房间叫醒了乔治。乔治随即叫醒了还在沙发上睡觉的马里昂。马里昂带着三岁的西尔维娅去屋外安全的地方。珍妮在阁楼楼梯底部疯狂大喊，让楼上的七个孩子快下来。火势蔓延得极快，已经开始吞噬楼梯了。经过漫长得仿佛一个世纪的煎熬，约翰和小乔治终于跑了下来。他们的头发都被火焰烧焦了。与此同时，老乔治试图给当地消防局打电话，却发现索德家的电话线已经断了。

7
00:05:54.000 --> 00:06:47.000
Marion sprinted to their closest neighbour who also tried to call but the phone went unanswered by the operator. Another neighbour who was still awake saw the Sotter House going up in flames and also attempted to phone the fire department. But again, there was no operator response. George Sr. was forced to retreat from the house when the flames and smoke became too intense. Four of his children and his wife were safe outside in the freezing winter night. But his five children who had been up late playing with their toys remained in the attic. Attempts to control the fire with water from the outside rain barrel proved fruitless. It was frozen solid.
马里昂飞奔去找最近的邻居，邻居也试图打电话，但接线员一直没有接听。另一个还没睡觉的邻居看到索德家陷入火海，也试图给消防局打电话。但同样，接线员没有任何回应。当火焰和浓烟变得极其猛烈时，老乔治被迫撤出了房子。他的四个孩子和妻子在冰冷的冬夜里安全地待在外面。但他的五个因为玩玩具玩得很晚而留在阁楼里的孩子却没有出来。用外面雨水桶里的水灭火的尝试证明是徒劳的。水已经冻成实心的了。

8
